   "description": "The 15q11.2 deletion or duplication in htis region involve 4 genes. The deletion is also known as Burnside-Butler syndrome (BBS) (MIM#615656). This region contains NIPA1 and NIPA2, two important magnesium transporters, which are active in the central nervous system. CYFIP1 is an important interactor with FMR1, which is the causative gene for fragile X syndrome (MIM#300624).",
   "hasBioChemEntityPart": [
