     "name": "15q13.3 microdeletion syndrome",
     "description": "A rare chromosomal anomaly characterized by a high risk for the occurrence of a wide range of neurodevelopmental anomalies including global developmental delay (DD), intellectual disability (ID), and behavioral issues of varying severity. 15q13.3 microdeletion does not lead to a clinically specific phenotype.",
     "sameAs": [
      "https://identifiers.org/mim:612001"
     ],
