   "description": "22q11.2 distal copy number variations (CNVs) are rare deletions or duplications located distal (telomeric) to the classic DiGeorge syndrome region, specifically between low copy repeats (LCR) D-E or D-F. They cause a distinct, highly variable syndrome with symptoms including developmental delay, speech difficulties, hypotonia, and mild dysmorphic features.",
